Guidelime.registerGuide([[
[D Quests for the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj \\ https://github.com/JanRK/Guidelime_DungeonQuests]
[N 60 40man Ahn Qiraj]
[NX 60 40man Blackwing Lair]

The Temple of Ahn'Qiraj is a 40-player raid behind the Scarab Wall in the far south-west of Silithus; its gate is west of the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj entrance, set into the same wall. Dungeon Journal has no entry for it; the entrance spot 24.4,87.5 Silithus is from QuestieDB's Forever dungeon list. Every quest here is optional: each starts from a raid drop and most turn in to the bronze dragons inside the temple. No Forever source says whether the Ahn'Qiraj gates are open (unverified); if they are shut the raid and these quests are not reachable. The road to Silithus passes level 48-63 mobs, including elites.

-- Left out: the Scepter of the Shifting Sands chain (8286 What Tomorrow Brings, 8288 Only One May Rise, 8730 Nefarius's Corruption, 8578 Scrying Goggles? No Problem!, 8301 and on to 8743 Bang a Gong!). Wowhead Forever has tooltips for these quests and Attune lists the chain, so it may exist on Forever. Left out, see the Ahn'Qiraj guide (a 30-quest world chain with a reputation grind and the one-time gate event); Questie hides 8743 under its AQ War Effort option. The Molten Core and Blackwing Lair guides point here for it.
-- Left out: the class set pieces (8544-8562, 8592-8596 bar 8595, 8602-8669) and the Cenarion Hold rings, cloaks and weapons (8556-8558, 8689-8712). They need Qiraji tokens and idols plus Brood of Nozdormu or Cenarion Circle reputation (Wowhead Forever tooltips list these needs); they are gear turn-ins, not dungeon steps.

-- Horde: Gadgetzan, Un'Goro, Silithus.
[A Horde] Make your way to Gadgetzan in Tanaris (the Shaper's Terrace guide walks there). At Bulkrek Ragefist, get the Gadgetzan flight path [P Gadgetzan] [G51.6,25.5 Tanaris]
-- Alliance: Gadgetzan, Un'Goro, Silithus.
[A Alliance] Make your way to Gadgetzan in Tanaris (the Shaper's Terrace guide walks there). At Bera Stonehammer, get the Gadgetzan flight path [P Gadgetzan] [G51.0,29.3 Tanaris] \\ A Gadgetzan Enforcer (level 57) stands nearby.

-- Both factions.
[A Horde] North-west out of Gadgetzan [G51.6,25.5 Tanaris][G41.1,27.6 Tanaris] [OC]
[A Alliance] North-west out of Gadgetzan [G51.0,29.3 Tanaris][G41.1,27.6 Tanaris] [OC]
Up toward the Un'Goro rim [G41.1,27.6 Tanaris][G37.6,22.4 Tanaris][G35.0,17.2 Tanaris][G31.5,11.9 Tanaris][G28.0,7.5 Tanaris] [OC] \\ Sandfury trolls (elite, level 42-45) stand outside Zul'Farrak near 38-41,21-28: keep east of them.
Down into Un'Goro Crater and west along the northern rim [G67.8,4.0 Un'Goro Crater][G64.6,4.1 Un'Goro Crater][G61.3,6.7 Un'Goro Crater][G58.5,8.9 Un'Goro Crater][G55.3,8.6 Un'Goro Crater][G45.2,5.8 Un'Goro Crater] [OC] \\ Un'Goro raptors and devilsaurs (level 48-55) roam the crater floor; Pterrordaxes (50-52) fly along this rim.
At Gryfe in Marshal's Refuge, get the Marshal's Refuge flight path [P Marshal's Refuge] [G45.2,5.8 Un'Goro Crater]
West along the northern edge of the crater to the Silithus pass [G45.2,5.8 Un'Goro Crater][G45.5,8.7 Un'Goro Crater][G39.0,10.2 Un'Goro Crater][G32.5,12.2 Un'Goro Crater][G19.3,13.1 Un'Goro Crater][G9.5,20.0 Un'Goro Crater] [OC] \\ Un'Goro beasts (level 48-55) and the Fire Plume Ridge elementals west of the Refuge.
Through the pass into Silithus and on to Cenarion Hold [G9.5,20.0 Un'Goro Crater][G60.9,24.6 Silithus][G54.0,29.8 Silithus] [OC] \\ Stonelash scorpids, Dredge mobs and Silithid Darters (level 54-60) along the road; Darters (60) also roam by Cenarion Hold.
[A Horde] Round the south side of Cenarion Hold to the wind rider master [G54.0,29.8 Silithus][G54.5,37.0 Silithus][G51.0,38.3 Silithus][G48.8,36.7 Silithus] [OC]
[A Horde] At Runk Windtamer, get the Cenarion Hold flight path [P Cenarion Hold] [G48.8,36.7 Silithus]
[A Alliance] Round the south side of Cenarion Hold to the hippogryph master [G54.0,29.8 Silithus][G54.5,37.0 Silithus][G51.0,38.3 Silithus][G50.7,34.6 Silithus] [OC]
[A Alliance] At Cloud Skydancer, get the Cenarion Hold flight path [P Cenarion Hold] [G50.7,34.6 Silithus]
[A Alliance] Back to the south gate of Cenarion Hold [G50.7,34.6 Silithus][G51.0,38.3 Silithus] [OC]
[A Horde] Back to the south gate of Cenarion Hold [G48.8,36.7 Silithus][G51.0,38.3 Silithus] [OC]
South out of Cenarion Hold and across the open sand to the Scarab Wall [G51.0,38.3 Silithus][G50.8,43.6 Silithus][G49.9,48.8 Silithus][G49.9,69.5 Silithus][G48.8,72.9 Silithus] [OC] \\ Emissary Roman'khan (elite 63) stands at 48.8,58.1 near this line; Hive'Ashi Stingers and Swarmers (elite 57-58) roam around 48.5,44-50.
South-west along the wall to the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj gate [G48.8,72.9 Silithus][G24.4,87.5 Silithus] [OC] \\ A Hive'Regal Spitfire (elite 59-60) near 49.5,73.3 and Grubthor (elite 58) near 44.4,80.8; Setis (elite 61) near 29.6,86.6, close to the gate.

-- Inside the temple. QuestieDB gives no spots inside: Andorgos and Kandrostrasz stand with the bronze dragons near the temple entrance (per the 8784 Wowhead Forever tooltip; unverified on Forever); Caelestrasz, Arygos and Merithra of the Dream appear after C'Thun (unverified on Forever).
Optional: if a Qiraji Lord's Insignia drops, take it to Kandrostrasz for [QA8579 Mortal Champions] and turn in [QT8579 Mortal Champions] \\ For each further insignia he offers [QA8595 Mortal Champions] [QT8595 Mortal Champions] (repeatable).
Optional: if an Ancient Qiraji Artifact drops, right-click it to start [QA8784 Secrets of the Qiraji] and give it to Andorgos [QT8784 Secrets of the Qiraji]
Optional: after C'Thun, if you win the Eye of C'Thun, right-click it to start [QA8801 C'Thun's Legacy] and give it to Caelestrasz [QT8801 C'Thun's Legacy]. He gives [QA8802 The Savior of Kalimdor]
Optional: Arygos offers [QA8789 Imperial Qiraji Armaments] and Merithra of the Dream [QA8790 Imperial Qiraji Regalia]. Each needs the Imperial Qiraji item from C'Thun and 3 Elementium Ore [QT8789 Imperial Qiraji Armaments] [QT8790 Imperial Qiraji Regalia]

